# No unsolicited branches

Do **not** create, switch to, or check out a new feature/topic branch unless the user explicitly authorizes it with the exact phrase **Make a branch** (case-insensitive is fine).

## Forbidden without that phrase

- `git checkout -b …`
- `git switch -c …`
- Creating a branch because a Linear/GitHub ticket suggests a `gitBranchName`
- Creating a branch “to keep master clean” or before starting a ticket

## Allowed without that phrase

- Work on the **current** branch (including `master` / `main`)
- Inspect branches (`git branch`, `git status`, `git log`)
- Commit / PR only when the user separately asks for those

## If a ticket suggests a branch name

Note the suggested name in the reply and keep working on the current branch until the user says **Make a branch**.
